    {
      "id": "macbeth/sceneIII_20.6/p@89083",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "LENNOX.\nAnd that well might\nAdvise him to a caution, t’ hold what distance\nHis wisdom can provide. Some holy angel\nFly to the court of England, and unfold\nHis message ere he come, that a swift blessing\nMay soon return to this our suffering country\nUnder a hand accurs’d!",
